request.description:
Customer Confirms Work: Verify customer can confirm and payment moves to CONFIRMED

POST [http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/{{transactionId}}/confirm](http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/{{transactionId}}/confirm)  
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

**Expected Response (200 OK):**

{  
"transactionId": 1,  
"status": "CONFIRMED",  
"completedAt": "2025-12-22T11:00:00",  
...  
}

Release Payment: Verify payment is released to provider (PAID state)

POST: [http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/{{transactionId}}/release](http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/{{transactionId}}/release)  
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

**Expected Response (200 OK):**

{  
"transactionId": 1,  
"status": "PAID",  
"completedAt": "2025-12-22T11:00:00",  
...  
}

Useless endpoint after creating the Dispute Core System

Open Dispute: Test dispute flow instead of confirm  
POST [http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/{{transactionId}}/dispute](http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/{{transactionId}}/dispute)  
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

**Expected Response (200 OK):**

{  
"transactionId": 1,  
"status": "DISPUTED",  
"completedAt": "2025-12-22T11:00:00",  
...  
}

